A14: add a separately adjustable Realtek pre-idle diagnostic hold

Apply after the Realtek idle-hold patch with its native-HPD correction.
Share its software-connection, exact branch identity, active DSC and HBR3
checks. The new hold runs before PUSH_IDLE, only if idle has not already
completed. Default zero; root-writable and capped at one second per disable.

Keep the earlier post-idle parameter at zero for the first comparison. The
new helper only reads the branch identity, logs and sleeps; it does not send
a video-stop or power command. Normal PUSH_IDLE and cleanup follow it.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_ctrl.c
@@ -28,6 +28,12 @@
 #include "dp_link.h"
 #include "dp_tu_calc.h"
 #include <drm/drm_fixed.h>
+
+/* Separate diagnostic hold while the compressed stream is still running. */
+static unsigned int a14_dp_realtek_pre_idle_hold_ms;
+module_param(a14_dp_realtek_pre_idle_hold_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(a14_dp_realtek_pre_idle_hold_ms,
+	"Hold Realtek A14 DSC links before PUSH_IDLE; milliseconds, capped at 1000, 0 disables");
 
 /* Diagnostic delay after source idle, before DPU/DSC/FEC teardown. */
 static unsigned int a14_dp_realtek_idle_hold_ms;
@@ -842,15 +848,19 @@
 	drm_dbg_dp(ctrl->drm_dev, "mainlink off\n");
 }
 
-/* Only connected bridge disable calls this, before the DPU is disabled. */
-void msm_dp_ctrl_a14_realtek_idle_hold(struct msm_dp_ctrl *msm_dp_ctrl)
